  "content": "Here is the step-by-step exact integer arithmetic for the given problem.\n\n**Given:**\n*   $a = 137$\n*   $b = 29$\n*   $c = 11$\n\n**Expression:**\n$$(a \\cdot b + c^3) - (a - b) \\cdot c$$\n\n### Step 1: Compute the product $a \\cdot b$\n$$137 \\times 29$$\n\nBreakdown:\n$$137 \\times 29 = 137 \\times (30 - 1)$$\n$$= (137 \\times 30) - (137 \\times 1)$$\n$$= 4110 - 137$$\n$$= 3973$$\n\nSo, **$a \\cdot b = 3973$**.\n\n### Step 2: Compute the cube $c^3$\n$$11^3 = 11 \\times 11 \\times 11$$\n$$11 \\times 11 = 121$$\n$$121 \\times 11 = 1331$$\n\nSo, **$c^3 = 1331$**.\n\n### Step 3: Compute the sum $(a \\cdot b + c^3)$\n$$3973 + 1331$$\n\nBreakdown:\n$$3973 + 1331 = 5304$$\n\nSo, **$a \\cdot b + c^3 = 5304$**.\n\n### Step 4: Compute the difference $(a - b)$\n$$137 - 29$$\n\nBreakdown:\n$$137 - 29 = 108$$\n\nSo, **$a - b = 108$**.\n\n### Step 5: Compute the product $(a - b) \\cdot c$\n$$108 \\times 11$$\n\nBreakdown:\n$$108 \\times 11 = 108 \\times (10 + 1)$$\n$$= (108 \\times 10) + (108 \\times 1)$$\n$$= 1080 + 108$$\n$$= 1",
